The attached image, corresponding to Fig. 6 and Fig. 7 in the PDF, illustrates Nano-11's ability to activate dendritic cells in vitro. Panel A shows that Nano-11 (black line) increases the expression of costimulatory molecules CD80 and CD86 on dendritic cells, compared to the medium control (gray line), although CD40 expression remains similar. Panel B and C demonstrate Nano-11's dose-dependent induction of IL-12p40 secretion and, especially when primed with LPS, robust IL-1β secretion, which surpasses that induced by aluminum hydroxide adjuvant at the highest dose. Panel D's immunoblot confirms that the secreted IL-1β is the active 17 kD form. These findings collectively indicate Nano-11's immunostimulatory properties on dendritic cells.